1
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:04,971
Meat?

2
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:07,874
Or fish?

3
00:00:09,309 --> 00:00:12,212
Meat or fish? Which one?

4
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:14,381
You can't decide?

5
00:00:23,156 --> 00:00:27,160
When you can't decide, do something crazy.

6
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:28,461
Unbelievable...

7
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:33,233
If you do, you'll find the answer.

8
00:00:37,504 --> 00:00:39,339
This is the answer.

9
00:00:43,076 --> 00:00:44,010
Try it.

10
00:00:44,744 --> 00:00:45,745
Seriously?

11
00:00:45,812 --> 00:00:47,947
This is Japan's best diner.

12
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,917
Delicious food is delicious
even if you mix it.

13
00:00:52,152 --> 00:00:53,019
I see.

14
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:56,523
Screw you!

15
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:01,194
Hey, lady.

16
00:01:02,128 --> 00:01:03,463
The bill.

17
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:07,767
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

18
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:10,603
Thanks.

19
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:17,610
<i>In 2014, medical establishments collapsed</i>
<i>and became more corrupt.</i>

20
00:01:18,878 --> 00:01:21,047
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

21
00:01:21,681 --> 00:01:25,118
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

22
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:28,588
Mr. Tendo.

23
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:32,092
We at Seikyo University
research medical care

24
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:35,528
are working day and night for
this hospital's prosperity.

25
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:39,332
In the past month, we've turned in

26
00:01:39,399 --> 00:01:42,602
far more clinical reports
than Totei University.

27
00:01:42,669 --> 00:01:44,337
No, I believe

28
00:01:44,404 --> 00:01:46,406
quality surpasses quantity.

29
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:49,008
The reports that we turned in

30
00:01:49,075 --> 00:01:52,745
are better in quality than
the numbers they boast.

31
00:01:52,812 --> 00:01:56,015
Again with the futile arguments.

32
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:02,222
Unifying the two posts
of surgical director

33
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,623
is urgent.

34
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:06,392
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

35
00:02:06,726 --> 00:02:08,962
<i>Japan announced to</i>

36
00:02:09,395 --> 00:02:11,865
<i>export state of the art medical services</i>

37
00:02:11,931 --> 00:02:13,900
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

38
00:02:14,834 --> 00:02:15,702
Excuse me?

39
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:20,039
I will have one of you

40
00:02:22,876 --> 00:02:24,444
leave your position as director.

41
00:02:27,247 --> 00:02:28,515
An election?

42
00:02:29,916 --> 00:02:30,917
No.

43
00:02:31,951 --> 00:02:34,387
Then how will you choose?

44
00:02:39,225 --> 00:02:41,361
These are the charts

45
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,696
for the Bureau Chief of a ministry.

46
00:02:44,531 --> 00:02:48,535
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>
<i>of the strong preying on the weak.</i>

47
00:02:48,601 --> 00:02:49,602
PATIENT NAME: IGARASHI

48
00:02:50,203 --> 00:02:51,104
How are you?

49
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:52,105
I won't touch you.

50
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:53,006
Sir!

51
00:03:03,816 --> 00:03:04,751
Hello.

52
00:03:04,817 --> 00:03:06,953
His illness is colon cancer.

53
00:03:07,954 --> 00:03:09,355
Stage III.

54
00:03:10,256 --> 00:03:14,661
Mr. Igarashi is from the Ministry
of Economy, Trade and Industry,

55
00:03:14,727 --> 00:03:18,665
which promotes the export
of Japanese healthcare.

56
00:03:19,098 --> 00:03:22,669
- Don't tell me...
- That's how you'll decide?

57
00:03:25,638 --> 00:03:26,539
Excuse me.

58
00:03:26,973 --> 00:03:28,074
What's the matter?

59
00:03:28,141 --> 00:03:29,576
I'm here for Dr. Dangozaka.

60
00:03:30,677 --> 00:03:31,578
What is it?

61
00:03:32,946 --> 00:03:36,082
Mr. Tanaka of the general ward is missing.

62
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:40,320
Do you know where Mr. Tanaka is?

63
00:03:40,386 --> 00:03:42,288
I don't know.

64
00:03:42,355 --> 00:03:45,325
We were playing
a game of Shogi until just now.

65
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,963
I'm having people search,

66
00:03:50,029 --> 00:03:51,231
but we can't find him.

67
00:03:52,031 --> 00:03:53,233
Would you come?

68
00:03:57,870 --> 00:04:00,740
I cannot leave right now.

69
00:04:00,807 --> 00:04:02,875
We're having an important meeting.

70
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:06,212
Contact me as soon as you find him.

71
00:04:08,181 --> 00:04:09,082
I understand.

72
00:04:13,686 --> 00:04:14,754
Something else?

73
00:04:16,556 --> 00:04:17,657
Dr. Dangozaka,

74
00:04:18,191 --> 00:04:20,326
you are his physician in charge.

75
00:04:21,661 --> 00:04:23,529
You'll be responsible.

76
00:04:26,232 --> 00:04:30,203
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

77
00:04:30,703 --> 00:04:34,440
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

78
00:04:34,507 --> 00:04:35,842
Stop following me.

79
00:04:37,844 --> 00:04:40,580
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

80
00:04:43,349 --> 00:04:44,284
Find him?

81
00:04:44,350 --> 00:04:45,451
Not yet.

82
00:04:45,518 --> 00:04:46,586
Where did he go?

83
00:04:46,653 --> 00:04:49,355
I said stop following me.

84
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:50,623
Mr. Tanaka!

85
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,795
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

86
00:04:56,429 --> 00:04:59,499
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

87
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:04,671
<i>Her medical license</i>
<i>and experience are her only weapons.</i>

88
00:05:04,737 --> 00:05:06,205
I'll get mad!

89
00:05:06,706 --> 00:05:08,374
Mr. Tanaka, I can see you.

90
00:05:10,243 --> 00:05:11,978
This old man's a patient?

91
00:05:13,079 --> 00:05:16,182
You cannot sneak out of the hospital.

92
00:05:18,718 --> 00:05:20,653
She kidnapped me.

93
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:25,958
I was so scared.

94
00:05:26,025 --> 00:05:28,861
Then give me some ransom money.

95
00:05:28,928 --> 00:05:30,096
Stop it.

96
00:05:31,230 --> 00:05:35,234
Mr. Tanaka, please return to your room.

97
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:40,840
Gosh. I got yelled at.

98
00:05:40,907 --> 00:05:41,741
Let's go.

99
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:46,846
Lady doctor.

100
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:49,215
Kidnap me again.

101
00:05:49,282 --> 00:05:50,583
I won't do that.

102
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:55,388
Unbelievable.

103
00:05:55,455 --> 00:05:58,458
I apologize for the trouble.

104
00:05:59,325 --> 00:06:00,326
Oh no!

105
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:20,780
We got this patient.

106
00:06:21,514 --> 00:06:22,515
Bye.

107
00:06:28,254 --> 00:06:29,355
Oh no...

108
00:06:31,824 --> 00:06:35,862
I'm starving. I want my lunch money back.

109
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:38,464
I seriously should've asked for a ransom.

110
00:06:39,932 --> 00:06:42,435
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon...</i>

111
00:06:42,502 --> 00:06:44,537
Damn it.

112
00:06:44,604 --> 00:06:47,940
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

113
00:07:16,636 --> 00:07:18,271
Mr. Ebina's team

114
00:07:18,337 --> 00:07:21,107
will handle the operation.

115
00:07:21,808 --> 00:07:23,075
Please rest assured.

116
00:07:25,077 --> 00:07:26,446
I'm glad I'm in good hands.

117
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,481
I'm counting on you.

118
00:07:29,482 --> 00:07:30,316
Yes.

119
00:07:31,184 --> 00:07:32,618
You know,

120
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:35,354
having to rest
at this busy time really hurts.

121
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:39,859
It's about setting up
a hospital in Indonesia, yes?

122
00:07:40,827 --> 00:07:41,694
Yes.

123
00:07:42,662 --> 00:07:45,431
Germany and France are on it.

124
00:07:45,498 --> 00:07:49,435
We'd really like to win this one.

125
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:52,104
Kaji,

126
00:07:52,171 --> 00:07:54,207
colon cancer is your specialty.

127
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:58,845
Exhibit your virtuosity as
the wizard of laparoscopy.

128
00:07:58,911 --> 00:08:00,146
Leave it to me.

129
00:08:00,213 --> 00:08:02,648
I will get you the director's seat.

130
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:05,117
Good man.

131
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,623
What should I do?

132
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:12,191
Who are you?

133
00:08:12,625 --> 00:08:14,427
Dr. Kaji,

134
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,796
we're still doing this? I'm Mamoru Hara.

135
00:08:16,863 --> 00:08:19,732
Hara, you'll work right under the top guy.

136
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:21,267
The 1st assistant.

137
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:23,469
Please assist Kaji.

138
00:08:23,536 --> 00:08:24,704
Yes, sir.

139
00:08:24,770 --> 00:08:27,139
The East has already won this.

140
00:08:27,206 --> 00:08:29,075
Let's see how badly we can beat them.

141
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:31,744
"Change and challenge."

142
00:08:31,811 --> 00:08:34,013
"Change and challenge."

143
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,648
Yeah, yeah.

144
00:08:35,715 --> 00:08:38,317
TOMOKO SEKIGAHARA, SECRETARY

145
00:08:45,992 --> 00:08:46,859
Sekigahara.

146
00:08:47,293 --> 00:08:48,160
Yes?

147
00:08:49,328 --> 00:08:51,097
- Do you have a minute?
- Yes?

148
00:08:53,599 --> 00:08:57,236
It's confidential,
so I wanted to talk in private.

149
00:08:58,471 --> 00:08:59,605
What is it?

150
00:09:01,073 --> 00:09:04,610
I will soon become the only director.

151
00:09:05,177 --> 00:09:06,679
It's pretty much decided.

152
00:09:07,947 --> 00:09:09,882
Well, congratulations.

153
00:09:12,451 --> 00:09:15,221
And so, I know it's a little early,

154
00:09:16,088 --> 00:09:17,356
but let's celebrate.

155
00:09:18,958 --> 00:09:19,926
Anything you want?

156
00:09:20,593 --> 00:09:22,261
You'll buy me something?

157
00:09:22,328 --> 00:09:25,831
Well, let's have dinner first.

158
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,367
How about steak?

159
00:09:29,335 --> 00:09:31,070
I like steak...

160
00:09:32,171 --> 00:09:33,039
Great.

161
00:09:33,539 --> 00:09:37,376
Then let's meet at
Sukiyabashi at 7 tonight.

162
00:09:41,881 --> 00:09:42,748
Daimon!

163
00:09:42,815 --> 00:09:44,550
You were listening?

164
00:09:44,617 --> 00:09:45,785
I was not.

165
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,423
Sukiyabashi, huh?

166
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:55,494
The steak there is delicious.

167
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:57,396
Rare steak.

168
00:09:58,197 --> 00:09:59,298
Which restaurant?

169
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:02,969
Because of that runaway patient,

170
00:10:03,035 --> 00:10:06,038
the East took an important operation.

171
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:08,140
If we don't get it back,

172
00:10:08,207 --> 00:10:10,476
you and I are both done for.

173
00:10:11,143 --> 00:10:13,012
Don't say something so scary.

174
00:10:13,913 --> 00:10:16,782
Isn't there a way?

175
00:10:16,849 --> 00:10:18,417
Anything?

176
00:10:20,152 --> 00:10:21,754
How about this for a plan?

177
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:26,359
I'll be an assistant at the surgery

178
00:10:26,425 --> 00:10:28,260
and take over the surgeon's position.

179
00:10:28,861 --> 00:10:31,397
That way, the credit will be ours...

180
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:34,934
Yes. That's right.

181
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:36,969
Leave it to me.

182
00:10:37,536 --> 00:10:39,772
I will bring victory to the West.

183
00:10:41,273 --> 00:10:42,241
I refuse.

184
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:43,509
Why?

185
00:10:43,576 --> 00:10:46,012
We can do the surgery perfectly

186
00:10:46,078 --> 00:10:47,880
without the West's help.

187
00:10:48,714 --> 00:10:50,816
As I mentioned before,

188
00:10:50,883 --> 00:10:53,185
we'll perform

189
00:10:53,252 --> 00:10:56,455
a laparoscopic right
hemicolectomy for Mr. Igarashi.

190
00:10:56,889 --> 00:10:57,757
That's all.

191
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:05,564
Good job refusing.

192
00:11:05,631 --> 00:11:07,733
We will taste victory ourselves.

193
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:09,268
I'm sorry.

194
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:10,202
About what?

195
00:11:12,204 --> 00:11:13,439
The second case is

196
00:11:13,506 --> 00:11:15,808
Shingo Tanaka, 75 years old.

197
00:11:16,642 --> 00:11:21,047
He has right upper lobe
lung adenocarcinoma stage IA.

198
00:11:21,113 --> 00:11:23,549
The surgeon is Dr. Dangozaka.

199
00:11:24,717 --> 00:11:26,018
Please speak.

200
00:11:33,426 --> 00:11:37,797
A CT scan showed that
the right lung's upper lobe S1b

201
00:11:37,863 --> 00:11:42,001
has a lobular nodule that's 2cm large.

202
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:44,370
Our case is much greater.

203
00:11:44,437 --> 00:11:45,504
No contest.

204
00:11:45,571 --> 00:11:46,839
Nothing to worry about.

205
00:11:46,906 --> 00:11:48,674
- Let's play our own game.
- Yes.

206
00:11:49,241 --> 00:11:52,044
Here is the right upper lobe bronchus.

207
00:11:52,812 --> 00:11:56,482
A normal divergence
from the main bronchus.

208
00:11:56,549 --> 00:12:00,219
The biopsy shows it's an adenocarcinoma.

209
00:12:03,322 --> 00:12:04,356
I propose

210
00:12:04,824 --> 00:12:11,363
a low invasive complete thoracoscopic
right lung upper lobe resection.

211
00:12:11,430 --> 00:12:13,766
Show me the images again.

212
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:24,910
Mr. Tendo, I actually
have another proposition.

213
00:12:24,977 --> 00:12:26,112
Yes?

214
00:12:27,613 --> 00:12:33,152
I would like for Dr. Ebina of
the East to help for this surgery.

215
00:12:34,019 --> 00:12:34,854
Me?

216
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:38,224
It's an easy operation

217
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:42,027
that doesn't require
Dr. Ebina to go through the trouble.

218
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:43,329
However...

219
00:12:44,864 --> 00:12:49,902
Because it is easy, the East
and West should cooperate for it.

220
00:12:49,969 --> 00:12:55,908
Cooperating for an operation
like this will lead to

221
00:12:55,975 --> 00:12:57,977
the conflict between us being resolved.

222
00:12:58,043 --> 00:13:00,312
I truly believe so.

223
00:13:05,518 --> 00:13:08,420
That is a great idea.
I would love to help.

224
00:13:08,487 --> 00:13:09,822
He accepted.

225
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:12,424
He's being too full of himself.

226
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:14,660
I understand.

227
00:13:16,762 --> 00:13:20,800
For this operation,
Dr. Dangozaka and Dr. Ebina,

228
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:23,569
the two directors will be in charge.

229
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,171
Thank you, sir.

230
00:13:25,237 --> 00:13:26,972
Will a thoracoscopy do?

231
00:13:30,709 --> 00:13:32,478
How rude!

232
00:13:32,545 --> 00:13:35,748
Dr. Dangozaka is a thoracoscopy expert.

233
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:38,083
Show me the images again.

234
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:40,186
How dare you?

235
00:13:40,252 --> 00:13:41,720
Idiot. I'll smack you!

236
00:13:43,856 --> 00:13:46,525
Achi, don't call her an idiot.

237
00:13:46,892 --> 00:13:48,928
Smacking her is worse.

238
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:53,532
- I apologize.
- Sorry.

239
00:13:53,599 --> 00:13:55,568
You idiot. I know.

240
00:13:56,368 --> 00:13:59,572
Dr. Daimon, you can be an assistant.

241
00:14:00,406 --> 00:14:05,010
You can see the great work
of the two surgical directors.

242
00:14:05,077 --> 00:14:06,712
An assistant?

243
00:14:06,779 --> 00:14:08,647
Is that alright, Dr. Ebina?

244
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:09,882
Of course.

245
00:14:10,549 --> 00:14:11,383
Daimon.

246
00:14:12,384 --> 00:14:15,421
You will learn many things from us.

247
00:14:19,325 --> 00:14:20,492
Yes, sir.

248
00:15:03,736 --> 00:15:04,937
I can see you.

249
00:15:08,474 --> 00:15:10,009
You found me.

250
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,511
Are you cold, Mr. Igarashi?

251
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,914
Help! I'm being kidnapped again.

252
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:16,081
Hey!

253
00:15:16,148 --> 00:15:18,617
Does this hospital just accept anyone?

254
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:25,124
Such good care. Unlike me.

255
00:15:25,190 --> 00:15:26,859
I don't discriminate.

256
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:30,095
That's how doctors should be.

257
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:33,132
Going home?

258
00:15:33,198 --> 00:15:34,233
It's 5pm.

259
00:15:34,633 --> 00:15:35,768
Do me a favor.

260
00:15:35,834 --> 00:15:37,469
No kidnappings.

261
00:15:37,536 --> 00:15:39,838
I'll pay you as much as you want.

262
00:15:46,712 --> 00:15:50,749
Tempura bowl, cutlet bowl,
and chicken and egg bowl.

263
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:53,986
You'll treat me to all this?

264
00:15:54,053 --> 00:15:55,921
Who said I'd treat you?

265
00:15:57,923 --> 00:16:00,960
I'm really hungry.

266
00:16:02,227 --> 00:16:06,198
But the cafeteria lady won't serve me.

267
00:16:07,666 --> 00:16:10,269
She watches me like that.

268
00:16:10,336 --> 00:16:12,738
Of course. Your surgery's tomorrow.

269
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:14,974
No dinner tonight.

270
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,042
How cruel.

271
00:16:17,109 --> 00:16:18,077
Deal with it.

272
00:16:26,318 --> 00:16:28,420
I can at least smell it, right?

273
00:16:29,088 --> 00:16:30,122
That's fine.

274
00:16:30,556 --> 00:16:31,690
Just a smell.

275
00:16:32,925 --> 00:16:34,593
You're nice.

276
00:16:44,903 --> 00:16:46,071
That's great.

277
00:16:47,806 --> 00:16:49,308
What do you do for a living?

278
00:16:50,042 --> 00:16:53,145
I farm-raise shrimp around the world.

279
00:16:53,212 --> 00:16:54,580
Business trips?

280
00:16:55,381 --> 00:16:57,116
I suppose.

281
00:16:57,182 --> 00:16:58,150
Must be hard.

282
00:16:58,217 --> 00:17:01,186
I have friends everywhere I go,

283
00:17:01,253 --> 00:17:02,688
so I don't get bored.

284
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:04,123
I see.

285
00:17:05,057 --> 00:17:06,425
Friends are great.

286
00:17:07,159 --> 00:17:09,228
They help you when you're in need.

287
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:14,967
To me, they're much more
important than money.

288
00:17:16,068 --> 00:17:17,569
I don't get it.

289
00:17:18,170 --> 00:17:22,374
I've never had lots of money or friends.

290
00:17:23,409 --> 00:17:25,577
What a lonely life.

291
00:17:29,915 --> 00:17:30,749
Hey...

292
00:17:32,418 --> 00:17:35,087
Will you let me do your operation?

293
00:17:35,587 --> 00:17:36,488
My operation?

294
00:17:36,555 --> 00:17:38,090
I can easily cure you.

295
00:17:44,329 --> 00:17:46,098
That I can't do.

296
00:17:46,165 --> 00:17:47,099
Why?

297
00:17:47,166 --> 00:17:50,135
I had a friend help me come here too.

298
00:17:50,202 --> 00:17:55,007
I used lots of connections,
and finally got into this hospital.

299
00:17:55,707 --> 00:17:58,310
I'm indebted to him and the hospital.

300
00:17:58,377 --> 00:17:59,912
Indebted?

301
00:17:59,978 --> 00:18:04,016
You can't live life without
feeling indebted to others.

302
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,555
Sorry.

303
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,326
Want a whiff, lady doctor?

304
00:18:14,393 --> 00:18:15,594
I want a bite.

305
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:20,632
<i>A general ward patient's surgery?</i>

306
00:18:20,699 --> 00:18:23,435
<i>You really were unlucky.</i>

307
00:18:23,502 --> 00:18:24,369
Why?

308
00:18:24,903 --> 00:18:29,475
From what I hear, a government VIP
is in the deluxe suite.

309
00:18:29,808 --> 00:18:31,910
Why didn't you get that job?

310
00:18:31,977 --> 00:18:33,779
Think of the money.

311
00:18:33,846 --> 00:18:36,148
Then go negotiate.

312
00:18:36,215 --> 00:18:37,449
You're my manager.

313
00:18:37,516 --> 00:18:40,419
Yeah. Akira, aren't you
slacking off lately?

314
00:18:40,486 --> 00:18:44,123
I see, you'll both blame me like that.

315
00:18:44,523 --> 00:18:45,858
Fine then.

316
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:49,094
Take this. "Double reach!"

317
00:18:49,862 --> 00:18:50,696
Here.

318
00:18:53,932 --> 00:18:54,766
Anyway,

319
00:18:54,833 --> 00:18:57,336
they're having just one director now?

320
00:18:57,669 --> 00:18:58,737
- Really?
- No clue.

321
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,206
It's most likely Dr. Ebina.

322
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,108
Seriously?

323
00:19:03,175 --> 00:19:04,009
Safe.

324
00:19:04,843 --> 00:19:08,447
Dr. Ebina of the East is
in charge of the VIP, right?

325
00:19:09,748 --> 00:19:10,816
In the end,

326
00:19:11,550 --> 00:19:16,655
those who stay quiet and win the favor
of their superiors win.

327
00:19:16,722 --> 00:19:19,758
It's the sad truth of a hired employee.

328
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:21,593
So true.

329
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:22,561
Safe.

330
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:27,166
I guess the only good thing about him

331
00:19:27,232 --> 00:19:30,269
is that he's not loose with women.

332
00:19:37,743 --> 00:19:38,977
Sekigahara?

333
00:19:39,044 --> 00:19:42,214
You never know.
You always hear of money and power

334
00:19:42,281 --> 00:19:47,386
making honest people go crazy.

335
00:19:47,452 --> 00:19:51,023
They usually just crash and burn.

336
00:19:52,457 --> 00:19:54,860
Michiko, crash and burn.

337
00:19:55,727 --> 00:19:56,562
Ron!

338
00:19:57,462 --> 00:19:59,831
That'll be 8,000 points.

339
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,936
No way!

340
00:20:04,002 --> 00:20:06,004
Michiko's last place again.

341
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:07,639
Let's play again.

342
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,575
We're done for today.

343
00:20:09,641 --> 00:20:12,411
I have to pick up Mai.

344
00:20:12,477 --> 00:20:14,980
Just one more game.

345
00:20:30,696 --> 00:20:32,030
Alright on time?

346
00:20:32,097 --> 00:20:32,931
I should go.

347
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,167
Mr. Tendo's dinner will end.

348
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:39,238
Hey.

349
00:20:40,839 --> 00:20:44,643
So the East and West,
which will be the director?

350
00:20:45,310 --> 00:20:46,678
They're both scums.

351
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:50,048
And we're the best hospital in Japan.

352
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:53,218
DR. EBINA

353
00:20:53,285 --> 00:20:54,386
It's ringing.

354
00:20:54,453 --> 00:20:55,520
It's fine.

355
00:21:08,834 --> 00:21:10,035
Once more.

356
00:21:15,874 --> 00:21:18,110
- Hello...
- <i>Your call cannot be answered.</i>

357
00:21:19,044 --> 00:21:20,279
The answering machine again.

358
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:23,548
Maybe something came up.

359
00:21:38,230 --> 00:21:39,731
Dr. Ebina!

360
00:21:39,798 --> 00:21:41,400
What are you doing?

361
00:21:41,466 --> 00:21:43,568
Oh... What about you guys?

362
00:21:43,635 --> 00:21:45,837
Celebrating for tomorrow's victory.

363
00:21:46,371 --> 00:21:47,572
Don't party too hard.

364
00:21:48,707 --> 00:21:50,709
"Change and challenge."

365
00:21:58,383 --> 00:21:59,551
I wasn't invited.

366
00:22:00,118 --> 00:22:02,454
Why wouldn't they invite their boss?

367
00:22:02,521 --> 00:22:03,889
"Change and..."

368
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:05,157
What is it?

369
00:22:05,223 --> 00:22:06,825
"Champion."

370
00:22:06,892 --> 00:22:08,260
"Change and champion."

371
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:09,161
It's "challenge."

372
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:30,982
Pull that side a little more.

373
00:22:31,049 --> 00:22:31,950
Yes.

374
00:22:52,571 --> 00:22:55,273
Sutures complete. Thank you.

375
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:56,641
Thank you.

376
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:59,811
That was a great operation. Well done.

377
00:23:00,445 --> 00:23:01,580
Thank you, sir.

378
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:09,755
I'll head to Mr. Tanaka's operation.

379
00:23:10,288 --> 00:23:11,289
Please do.

380
00:23:11,356 --> 00:23:14,760
I will give it my best. Excuse me.

381
00:23:31,309 --> 00:23:32,477
Let's play fair.

382
00:23:32,544 --> 00:23:33,545
Of course.

383
00:23:34,146 --> 00:23:36,381
- Let's do this.
- Yes.

384
00:23:48,193 --> 00:23:49,828
Let's start.

385
00:23:49,895 --> 00:23:51,830
I'm the surgeon.

386
00:23:51,897 --> 00:23:53,165
I'm the 1st assistant.

387
00:23:57,702 --> 00:24:04,276
We will begin complete thoracoscopic
right lung upper lobe resection.

388
00:24:04,342 --> 00:24:05,177
Let's begin.

389
00:24:05,243 --> 00:24:06,878
Yes.

390
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:11,082
Vitals. Blood pressure 120s,
pulse 80s and sinus.

391
00:24:11,149 --> 00:24:12,484
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

392
00:24:13,385 --> 00:24:14,252
- Gauze.
- Yes.

393
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,289
- Forceps.
- Yes.

394
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:23,562
Here for a general ward patient?

395
00:24:24,796 --> 00:24:29,267
I must make my final judgment
for the two directors.

396
00:24:30,602 --> 00:24:31,636
I see.

397
00:24:47,252 --> 00:24:49,754
Let's move to the separation.

398
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:52,390
- Yes. Change forceps.
- Yes.

399
00:25:05,103 --> 00:25:07,873
Right upper lobe removed.

400
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:10,475
Vitals are stable.

401
00:25:11,109 --> 00:25:13,378
Wonderful work, Dr. Dangozaka.

402
00:25:13,445 --> 00:25:14,412
Yeah, it's easy.

403
00:25:17,415 --> 00:25:21,453
Dr. Ebina, may I ask you to take over?

404
00:25:21,987 --> 00:25:23,688
Are you sure?

405
00:25:24,089 --> 00:25:28,193
We promised that
the East and West will cooperate.

406
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:30,595
Yes.

407
00:25:35,934 --> 00:25:39,437
- Give Dr. Ebina the hook electrocautery.
- Yes.

408
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:51,082
Let's begin.

409
00:26:05,697 --> 00:26:09,968
I'm worried about
the dead space after removal.

410
00:26:11,603 --> 00:26:12,871
Cutting the pulmonary ligament.

411
00:26:20,812 --> 00:26:25,483
Very well done. Your skills
are as great as I've heard.

412
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:26,751
Oh, please.

413
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:39,431
Blood pressure dropped to 80.

414
00:26:42,701 --> 00:26:45,470
This is bad. I'll take over.

415
00:26:49,307 --> 00:26:50,609
- Move!
- What?

416
00:26:52,711 --> 00:26:53,545
Damn you!

417
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:54,613
Change.

418
00:26:55,313 --> 00:26:56,448
- Compressor.
- Yes.

419
00:27:01,853 --> 00:27:04,456
It's the inferior pulmonary vein.
Blood loss?

420
00:27:04,522 --> 00:27:06,024
Over 300.

421
00:27:06,091 --> 00:27:07,225
Give him a transfusion.

422
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:08,560
Full transfusion. Starting now.

423
00:27:08,627 --> 00:27:10,562
- Yes, please begin.
- Yes.

424
00:27:10,629 --> 00:27:11,630
- Nurse.
- Yes.

425
00:27:12,597 --> 00:27:13,698
Stop it.

426
00:27:13,765 --> 00:27:16,434
He's my patient. Stay out.

427
00:27:18,403 --> 00:27:19,504
- Forceps.
- Yes.

428
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:31,016
Dr. Daimon again?

429
00:27:41,593 --> 00:27:44,062
Blood pressure back to 100s.

430
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:49,501
Damaged section confirmed.

431
00:27:49,567 --> 00:27:51,536
Repairing the vein.

432
00:27:51,603 --> 00:27:53,038
Hold that stump.

433
00:27:53,104 --> 00:27:54,205
Yes.

434
00:28:04,382 --> 00:28:05,784
- 6-0 nylon.
- Yes.

435
00:28:27,505 --> 00:28:30,475
Assistant, clean and close him.

436
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,609
Yes.

437
00:28:59,938 --> 00:29:01,673
Cheers!

438
00:29:06,611 --> 00:29:09,080
- Sir, congratulations.
- Congratulations.

439
00:29:09,147 --> 00:29:11,015
You did great. Thank you.

440
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:14,419
I sure was scared
when I heard what happened.

441
00:29:14,486 --> 00:29:15,520
That's true.

442
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:17,589
Damaged veins are common.

443
00:29:17,655 --> 00:29:19,257
So are pinches.

444
00:29:19,324 --> 00:29:23,762
But overcoming that pinch and winning
creates an even more emotional drama.

445
00:29:23,828 --> 00:29:25,663
Creator of drama!

446
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:29,267
I feel sorry for Dr. Dangozaka,

447
00:29:29,334 --> 00:29:31,035
but we're way ahead now.

448
00:29:31,102 --> 00:29:33,304
No need for pity.

449
00:29:33,671 --> 00:29:35,140
Drink all you want tonight.

450
00:29:35,206 --> 00:29:36,441
- Thank you.
- Thank you, sir.

451
00:29:37,909 --> 00:29:39,744
- Drink up.
- Thank you.

452
00:29:39,811 --> 00:29:42,013
Celebrations call for champagne.

453
00:29:42,347 --> 00:29:44,449
Drink more.

454
00:29:44,516 --> 00:29:45,383
Drink.

455
00:29:59,998 --> 00:30:04,869
<i>The fate of the West, Seikyo University,</i>

456
00:30:05,870 --> 00:30:07,605
<i>lies in your hands.</i>

457
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:10,408
If you lose,

458
00:30:10,775 --> 00:30:15,113
you and I will both be fired.

459
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:18,917
Understand,

460
00:30:19,584 --> 00:30:20,985
Dr. Dangozaka?

461
00:30:24,055 --> 00:30:24,923
Yes, sir.

462
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:34,966
I am victorious.

463
00:30:38,636 --> 00:30:40,171
I did it...

464
00:30:43,875 --> 00:30:45,610
Dr. Hiruma.

465
00:32:15,300 --> 00:32:16,267
I'm hung over.

466
00:32:18,903 --> 00:32:20,071
Dr. Ebina!

467
00:32:20,138 --> 00:32:20,972
What?

468
00:32:21,039 --> 00:32:22,106
It's Mr. Tanaka!

469
00:32:54,706 --> 00:32:55,807
What happened?

470
00:32:56,207 --> 00:32:58,810
I administered prednisolone.

471
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:06,084
This is really bad, Dr. Ebina.

472
00:33:25,303 --> 00:33:27,638
His lung is flipped.

473
00:33:28,339 --> 00:33:29,907
It's lung torsion.

474
00:33:29,974 --> 00:33:32,643
Look at what's happened.

475
00:33:33,144 --> 00:33:37,448
This is why I said not to interfere.

476
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:39,751
But I was shoved away.

477
00:33:40,118 --> 00:33:41,152
I'm sorry.

478
00:33:41,219 --> 00:33:42,787
I will speak to Daimon.

479
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:44,822
That's not it.

480
00:33:46,557 --> 00:33:50,294
Dr. Ebina, this is your responsibility.

481
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:56,768
Mr. Tendo.

482
00:33:57,368 --> 00:34:01,139
Will you please give permission
for surgery right now?

483
00:34:02,206 --> 00:34:04,008
I, Noboru Dangozaka,

484
00:34:04,075 --> 00:34:08,880
will take full responsibility
and cover for Dr. Ebina's mistake.

485
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:10,581
My mistake?

486
00:34:12,817 --> 00:34:14,318
Dr. Dangozaka,

487
00:34:15,686 --> 00:34:17,789
please perform another operation.

488
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:19,891
Yes, sir.

489
00:34:19,957 --> 00:34:21,059
Mr. Tendo.

490
00:34:22,293 --> 00:34:25,630
Dr. Daimon is operating on Mr. Tanaka.

491
00:34:26,631 --> 00:34:27,665
What?

492
00:34:38,543 --> 00:34:40,211
The blood pressure

493
00:34:40,278 --> 00:34:41,846
is stable from the dopamine.

494
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:43,514
- Got it. Scalpel.
- Yes.

495
00:34:48,453 --> 00:34:49,587
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

496
00:34:55,259 --> 00:34:56,194
That's my patient.

497
00:34:56,627 --> 00:35:00,898
Daimon, get out of there. Now!

498
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:04,068
I won't do that.

499
00:35:08,372 --> 00:35:09,340
Stop it, Daimon.

500
00:35:10,308 --> 00:35:12,510
If you fail, we're both finished.

501
00:35:12,910 --> 00:35:15,780
Unlike you, I don't fail.

502
00:35:15,847 --> 00:35:17,081
What?

503
00:35:25,823 --> 00:35:27,792
Lung torsion repositioned.

504
00:35:27,859 --> 00:35:28,893
- Hold this.
- Yes.

505
00:35:29,694 --> 00:35:31,696
We'll stitch for stabilization.

506
00:35:31,762 --> 00:35:32,930
- 4-0 nylon.
- Yes.

507
00:35:47,945 --> 00:35:50,748
Damn that woman.

508
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:51,949
I'll smack her.

509
00:35:53,518 --> 00:35:55,052
This is my surgery.

510
00:35:55,887 --> 00:35:57,221
I'm going to do it.

511
00:36:02,527 --> 00:36:03,761
Done.

512
00:36:04,162 --> 00:36:07,431
Blood loss 80. Blood pressure 120s,

513
00:36:07,498 --> 00:36:09,567
pulse 80s and sinus.

514
00:36:09,634 --> 00:36:11,836
- Thanks.
- Thank you.

515
00:36:13,004 --> 00:36:14,038
Nice job.

516
00:36:14,639 --> 00:36:15,540
Good job.

517
00:36:18,643 --> 00:36:20,444
Next time, I want an eel bowl.

518
00:36:22,547 --> 00:36:25,917
How dare you take my patient.

519
00:36:25,983 --> 00:36:28,653
Don't ever hide things!

520
00:36:54,812 --> 00:36:55,880
Daimon.

521
00:36:57,882 --> 00:36:59,617
What do you mean

522
00:37:00,184 --> 00:37:01,085
he hid something?

523
00:37:02,987 --> 00:37:04,589
Bronchial branch anomaly.

524
00:37:05,489 --> 00:37:06,324
Mr. Tanaka?

525
00:37:07,625 --> 00:37:09,527
He kept it a secret.

526
00:37:09,594 --> 00:37:13,497
A normal divergence
from the main bronchus.

527
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:17,101
The biopsy shows it's an adenocarcinoma.

528
00:37:17,902 --> 00:37:20,137
Show me the images again.

529
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:24,842
It was to make you
cut the pulmonary ligament.

530
00:37:26,677 --> 00:37:27,979
Dr. Ebina,

531
00:37:28,412 --> 00:37:30,881
may I ask you to take over?

532
00:37:36,153 --> 00:37:38,656
With a bronchial branch anomaly,

533
00:37:38,723 --> 00:37:41,392
there's more risk of lung torsion.

534
00:37:41,892 --> 00:37:46,330
And his plan was that
if torsion occurs, it would be my fault.

535
00:37:48,065 --> 00:37:48,933
That's right.

536
00:37:51,302 --> 00:37:53,371
He tried to kick me out
and crush the East.

537
00:37:54,639 --> 00:37:55,640
How cheap.

538
00:37:57,675 --> 00:37:59,443
You guys must be stupid

539
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:02,380
with your East and West stuff.

540
00:38:13,924 --> 00:38:15,793
RESIGNATION

541
00:38:16,594 --> 00:38:17,828
It's a resignation letter.

542
00:38:19,263 --> 00:38:23,200
Please date it and sign it.

543
00:38:26,103 --> 00:38:28,139
I'm fired?

544
00:38:28,205 --> 00:38:31,742
I saw your operation the other day.

545
00:38:34,378 --> 00:38:36,647
You did not perform surgery.

546
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:41,419
That's because Dr. Daimon pushed me away.

547
00:38:41,485 --> 00:38:43,921
You were not watching the patient.

548
00:38:47,558 --> 00:38:50,428
I don't understand what you mean.

549
00:38:50,494 --> 00:38:51,529
You...

550
00:38:54,165 --> 00:38:58,602
You only entered
the surgery room to trap Dr. Ebina.

551
00:39:03,574 --> 00:39:04,442
You are...

552
00:39:06,544 --> 00:39:07,445
Not a doctor.

553
00:39:10,948 --> 00:39:13,584
Leave this hospital immediately.

554
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:21,992
Why?

555
00:39:24,628 --> 00:39:28,032
You're firing
the head of Seikyo University?

556
00:39:48,619 --> 00:39:49,653
Forgive me.

557
00:40:01,966 --> 00:40:03,033
Dr. Dangozaka.

558
00:40:06,036 --> 00:40:07,738
No need to console me.

559
00:40:09,373 --> 00:40:10,741
That's not what I came for.

560
00:40:12,209 --> 00:40:13,077
But...

561
00:40:14,245 --> 00:40:15,746
I must tell you something.

562
00:40:17,448 --> 00:40:18,549
What?

563
00:40:21,452 --> 00:40:22,720
The strong don't win.

564
00:40:26,957 --> 00:40:28,526
The winners are the strong ones.

565
00:40:31,729 --> 00:40:36,600
You think you're some
emperor now? Unbelievable.

566
00:40:46,977 --> 00:40:47,812
What's this?

567
00:40:48,913 --> 00:40:50,047
Let's exchange uniforms.

568
00:40:53,751 --> 00:40:57,021
Forget it. Who would want that?

569
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:00,758
Move!

570
00:41:06,764 --> 00:41:07,631
Take that.

571
00:41:26,951 --> 00:41:28,018
Michiko Daimon.

572
00:41:29,053 --> 00:41:30,521
No "Doctor"?

573
00:41:30,588 --> 00:41:34,558
If you didn't get in the way,
the West would've won.

574
00:41:34,625 --> 00:41:37,394
I don't care about
doctors' wins or losses.

575
00:41:38,229 --> 00:41:40,364
The patient should be the winner.

576
00:41:42,566 --> 00:41:43,400
Listen.

577
00:41:45,102 --> 00:41:47,972
The West still has a monster.

578
00:41:49,039 --> 00:41:54,478
A terrifying monster who
won't settle for just crushing you.

579
00:41:58,382 --> 00:42:01,118
Don't think it's over.

580
00:42:03,921 --> 00:42:05,489
I'll be careful.

581
00:42:22,473 --> 00:42:23,641
Damn it!

582
00:42:24,408 --> 00:42:26,810
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

583
00:42:27,211 --> 00:42:29,947
<i>Her medical license and experience</i>

584
00:42:30,014 --> 00:42:31,582
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

585
00:42:37,955 --> 00:42:39,156
This is a bill.

586
00:42:44,194 --> 00:42:45,996
No melon?

587
00:42:46,964 --> 00:42:48,032
I'm sorry,

588
00:42:48,098 --> 00:42:50,901
it was a patient
from the general ward this time.

589
00:42:51,335 --> 00:42:54,204
So it's not a price
worth giving a melon for?

590
00:42:55,439 --> 00:42:56,307
Excuse me.

591
00:42:57,041 --> 00:42:58,409
1, 2, 3...

592
00:42:58,742 --> 00:43:00,244
It's expensive!

593
00:43:00,711 --> 00:43:02,446
Way above average.

594
00:43:02,513 --> 00:43:03,647
What do you think?

595
00:43:04,481 --> 00:43:08,085
I worked hard to cut down the price.

596
00:43:08,152 --> 00:43:11,522
You should've brought
a melon for this. 2 or 3.

597
00:43:11,589 --> 00:43:12,957
Next time, I will.

598
00:43:13,023 --> 00:43:13,958
Please do.

599
00:43:14,391 --> 00:43:16,627
I'm fine with the price.

600
00:43:17,094 --> 00:43:18,896
We will wire it to your account.

601
00:43:19,396 --> 00:43:20,497
Thank you.

602
00:43:20,998 --> 00:43:22,266
By the way,

603
00:43:22,733 --> 00:43:27,905
a patient is requesting to have Dr. Daimon
as their primary physician.

604
00:43:27,972 --> 00:43:29,540
Our Daimon?

605
00:43:30,874 --> 00:43:31,842
Who is it?

606
00:43:38,382 --> 00:43:39,216
Michiko!

607
00:43:39,883 --> 00:43:40,951
Hey, Akira.

608
00:43:41,018 --> 00:43:44,088
You got a general ward
patient to like you?

609
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:47,291
You should have
rich VIP patients like you.

610
00:43:47,358 --> 00:43:49,393
- What?
- Gosh.

611
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:52,029
You sure are a woman
who has no luck with men.

612
00:43:52,396 --> 00:43:56,200
That's terrible. Hey, Akira.

613
00:43:56,600 --> 00:43:57,568
Quiet!

614
00:43:57,635 --> 00:44:00,137
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

615
00:44:00,204 --> 00:44:03,674
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

616
00:44:08,779 --> 00:44:10,748
CLOSED FOR A PRIVATE EVENT

617
00:44:14,785 --> 00:44:16,186
I see.

618
00:44:16,253 --> 00:44:18,322
She refused.

619
00:44:19,056 --> 00:44:20,524
I'm sorry.

620
00:44:20,591 --> 00:44:22,459
Sorry for the trouble.

621
00:44:24,862 --> 00:44:26,196
I'll forget about it then.

622
00:44:27,798 --> 00:44:28,666
But

623
00:44:29,199 --> 00:44:32,102
I had an interesting
experience thanks to you.

624
00:44:33,103 --> 00:44:35,439
I'm glad that you are well now.

625
00:44:39,543 --> 00:44:42,312
About the hospital in Indonesia...

626
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:43,781
Yes.

627
00:44:43,847 --> 00:44:47,217
Bureau Chief Igarashi, was it?

628
00:44:47,918 --> 00:44:50,821
Some guy with just a big title is useless.

629
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:55,592
I used my connections and settled things.

630
00:44:57,428 --> 00:44:59,229
Germany and France will pull out.

631
00:44:59,963 --> 00:45:03,267
Japan will be building the hospital there.

632
00:45:03,667 --> 00:45:06,637
Only you could do
such a thing, Mr. Tanaka.

633
00:45:07,504 --> 00:45:09,039
Thank you.

634
00:45:10,941 --> 00:45:12,476
Now you

635
00:45:13,510 --> 00:45:15,713
even have a ministry indebted to you.

636
00:45:16,447 --> 00:45:18,082
But Mr. Tendo,

637
00:45:18,148 --> 00:45:20,284
what is it that you want?

638
00:45:23,020 --> 00:45:23,887
Money?

639
00:45:25,122 --> 00:45:26,056
Status?

640
00:45:27,524 --> 00:45:28,726
Or power?

641
00:45:32,029 --> 00:45:33,197
Power.

642
00:45:34,865 --> 00:45:37,568
But you already have plenty.

643
00:45:38,102 --> 00:45:40,938
The power to control a country.

644
00:45:48,178 --> 00:45:49,713
I like it!

645
00:45:56,754 --> 00:45:58,522
Doctor X...

646
00:46:00,958 --> 00:46:03,527
It might be a useful toy...

647
00:46:04,361 --> 00:46:05,195
Yes.

648
00:46:05,629 --> 00:46:09,166
<i>But that toy is a double-edged sword.</i>

649
00:46:10,033 --> 00:46:12,169
If you use it the wrong way,

650
00:46:12,870 --> 00:46:15,606
you'll be sliced.

651
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:18,375
A sword calls for a shield.

652
00:46:20,244 --> 00:46:22,212
I know very well.

653
00:46:49,540 --> 00:46:50,707
A secret?

654
00:46:50,774 --> 00:46:52,242
I smell money.

655
00:46:52,309 --> 00:46:54,511
Michiko Daimon doesn't fail.

656
00:46:54,578 --> 00:46:57,548
No matter what sort of
crime you've committed.

657
00:46:58,715 --> 00:47:00,184
I can't go on.

658
00:47:00,250 --> 00:47:01,351
What?

659
00:47:01,418 --> 00:47:03,353
Michiko Daimon, defeated...
